## Normative compatibility

Accepted D3.4 preserves full issuer component/history checks. D3.6 requires the same persistence worker, exact prior bytes/native identity and actual pinned ROOT8 predecessor for update; it explicitly excludes implicit ROOT06 migration. D3.7 prohibits historical fallback/truncation. D3.8 separates managed serialized subtotals from actual root resources. No accepted contract is changed or found contradictory: current adapter is an implementation boundary, not permission to reinterpret bytes. Issuer/C2 I/R/A/P, snapshots/pins and Model E remain unchanged.

INITIAL_BOOTSTRAP: only explicit virgin-store proof + administrative authorization + fully resolved candidate can prepare the corresponding path; not implemented/executed here. EXISTING_ROOT_UPDATE: requires actual CURRENT/base pin/CAS and same-history ROOT8 predecessor; no legacy ROOT06 conversion. Existing issuer content cannot be ignored, reset, made absent or re-encoded by this slice. No fabricated A/P/I/R or grants.

## Smallest next gate / directly scoped handoff

Before dependent wiring, review an exact format-aware adaptation of the SAME pending adapter, not another worker/root/journal: separate no-issuer D3 packet discriminator, factual native identity carried out-of-band from its owning native lease (never read from D3 R/predecessor), length-safe frozen previous/next/observed images, D3-specific completion that cannot touch issuer snapshots, and explicit rejection of any issuer-bearing/legacy root. Prove bootstrap virgin-store authorization separately and retain CURRENT/base-pin requirements for update. Preserve the existing ROOT06 branch byte-for-byte or prove equivalence. Do not extend this into carrier implementation or migration; those remain separate gates. The present task's section5 STOP prevents silently treating the issuer-dependent path as reusable.

No automatic normative change is requested. If supporting an existing issuer-bearing root is required, carrier/history integration must first be separately scoped; otherwise restrict a future implementation explicitly to proven no-issuer ROOT8 roots/new installations. Preserve multi-listener representation and reject unsupported runtime count rather than truncate. Never remove issuer_stage_prepared or substitute an all-zero issuer to force this path.

